6.4 If, at any time, the Engineer gives notice to the Contractor that the rate of progress is, in the Engineer's opinion, insufficient to ensure completion of the Works or any Section by the relevant Time for Completion, the Contractor shall, within fourteen (14) days of receipt of such notice, submit to the Engineer a revised Programme showing the measures the Contractor proposes to take to expedite progress. The Contractor shall not be entitled to additional payment for such measures, unless the delay is attributable to a cause for which the Employer is responsible under this Contract.

6.5 The Time for Completion of the Works, as stated in Appendix A, shall be twenty-four (24) months from the Commencement Date, subject to adjustment in accordance with Clause 6.6 and Clause 6.7.

6.6 The Contractor shall be entitled to an extension of the Time for Completion if and to the extent that completion is or will be delayed by any of the following causes:
(a) a Variation or any other change to the scope of the Works instructed by the Employer or the Engineer;
(b) a delay caused by the Employer, the Engineer, or any other contractor engaged by the Employer;
(c) exceptionally adverse climatic conditions, which for the purposes of this Contract shall mean conditions at the Site which are worse than those reasonably foreseeable at the date of this Contract and which materially affect the progress of the Works;
(d) any force majeure event as defined in Clause 17;
(e) any delay caused by the failure of the Employer to give access to the Site, to provide drawings, approvals, or information, or to satisfy any other obligation of the Employer under this Contract;
(f) any delay caused by the discovery of unforeseen physical conditions at the Site, including but not limited to buried structures, unexploded ordnance, or contaminated ground, which could not reasonably have been foreseen by an experienced contractor at the date of this Contract; or
(g) any other cause of delay which is expressly stated in this Contract to entitle the Contractor to an extension of time.

