6.7 Upon receipt of a notice of delay from the Contractor, given in accordance with Clause 6.8, the Engineer shall, within twenty-one (21) days of receipt of such notice and any supporting particulars, assess whether the Contractor is entitled to an extension of the Time for Completion and shall notify the Contractor and the Employer of the Engineer's determination. The Engineer shall grant an extension of time only to the extent that the delay is attributable to a cause listed in Clause 6.6 and only if the Contractor has complied with the notice requirements of Clause 6.8.

6.8 The Contractor shall give notice to the Engineer of any event or circumstance which the Contractor considers to be a cause of delay under Clause 6.6, within twenty-eight (28) days of the Contractor becoming aware, or of when the Contractor ought reasonably to have become aware, of such event or circumstance. The Contractor shall also submit to the Engineer, within forty-two (42) days of such notice, full supporting particulars of the delay, including the anticipated effect on the Programme and the estimated extension of time claimed. If the Contractor fails to give notice within the period stated, the Contractor shall not be entitled to an extension of time for the delay, unless the Engineer determines that the failure was due to circumstances beyond the Contractor's reasonable control and that the Employer has not been prejudiced by the failure.

Clause 9 – Insurance

9.1 Without limiting the Contractor’s liabilities or obligations under this Contract, the Contractor shall, at its own cost, take out and maintain the following insurances with insurers and in terms approved by the Employer, such approval not to be unreasonably withheld or delayed:

(a) Works Insurance, covering the Works, Plant, Materials and Contractor’s Documents for their full replacement value plus fifteen percent (15%) for overheads and profits, against all risks, for the full period from the Commencement Date until the issue of the Taking-Over Certificate for the whole of the Works;

(b) Third Party Insurance, covering the Contractor’s liability for death of or injury to any person (other than as covered by (c) below) or loss of or damage to any property (other than the Works) arising out of the execution of the Works, with a limit of not less than Five Million United States Dollars (US$5,000,000) per occurrence;

(c) Employer’s Liability and Workmen’s Compensation Insurance, covering all persons employed by the Contractor and its Subcontractors on or in connection with the Works, in accordance with the applicable laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria, including the Employee’s Compensation Act, 2010;

(d) Marine Cargo Insurance, covering all Plant, Materials and Contractor’s Equipment imported into Nigeria for the purpose of the Works, from the point of shipment to the site, on terms no less favourable than Institute Cargo Clauses (A), with a limit equal to the full insured value of the cargo plus ten percent (10%);

(e) Marine Third Party Liability Insurance, covering the Contractor’s liability arising from the use of vessels, tugs, barges and other floating equipment in connection with the Works, including but not limited to collision liability, damage to fixed or floating objects, and pollution, with a limit of not less than Two Million United States Dollars (US$2,000,000) per occurrence;

(f) Port Operations Liability Insurance, covering the Contractor’s activities within the Port of Onne, including but not limited to damage to port infrastructure, fenders, bollards, mooring dolphins and navigational aids, with a limit of not less than Three Million United States Dollars (US$3,000,000) per occurrence; and

(g) Professional Indemnity Insurance, covering the Contractor’s liability for errors, omissions or negligent acts in the performance of the design portion of the Works, with a limit of not less than One Million United States Dollars (US$1,000,000) per claim and in the aggregate.

9.2 The Contractor shall deliver to the Employer, prior to the Commencement Date, certificates of insurance evidencing that the insurances required under Clause 9.1 are in full force and effect. The Contractor shall also deliver certificates of renewal or other evidence of continued coverage not less than fourteen (14) days prior to the expiry of any such insurance.

9.3 The insurances shall be maintained with insurers of good repute and financial standing, and shall include a waiver of subrogation against the Employer, the Nigerian Ports Authority, their directors, officers, employees and agents, except to the extent of the Employer’s or the Nigerian Ports Authority’s own negligence or wilful misconduct.

9.4 If the Contractor fails to take out or maintain any of the insurances required under this Clause, the Employer may take out and maintain such insurance and pay the premiums due, and the Contractor shall reimburse the Employer the amount of such premiums, and such amount shall be deductible from any monies due or to become due to the Contractor under this Contract.

10. TERMINATION

10.1 The Employer may by written notice to the Contractor terminate this Contract in whole or in part, if the Contractor:

(a) becomes bankrupt or insolvent, or has a receiver or manager appointed over any part of its assets, or takes or suffers any similar action in consequence of debt;

(b) assigns or transfers this Contract or any part thereof without the prior written consent of the Employer, such consent not to be unreasonably withheld;

(c) fails to proceed with the Works with due diligence and expedition, and such failure continues for a period of fourteen (14) days after receipt of a written notice from the Employer specifying the nature of the failure;

(d) fails to comply with any final decision of the Engineer or the Dispute Adjudication Board within the time prescribed therein; or

(e) suspends the Works for a continuous period of twenty-eight (28) days otherwise than in accordance with Clause 12 (Suspension).

10.2 In the event of termination under Clause 10.1, the Employer may enter upon the Site, expel the Contractor therefrom, and take possession of all materials, Plant, Temporary Works and any other goods thereon, and may use them for the purpose of completing the Works or may sell them and apply the proceeds in accordance with Clause 10.4.

10.3 Upon termination under Clause 10.1, the Contractor shall, upon receipt of written notice from the Employer, promptly:

(a) cease all further work, except such work as the Employer may expressly authorise in writing for the sole purpose of protecting life or property or for the safety of the Works;

(b) deliver to the Employer all Contractor’s Documents, and any other documents or data relating to the Works, whether completed or in preparation;

(c) remove from the Site all Contractor’s Equipment, Temporary Works and unused materials within thirty (30) days, failing which the Employer may remove and store them at the Contractor’s risk and cost; and

(d) provide the Employer with a detailed statement of all amounts payable to the Contractor under Clause 10.4.

10.4 Upon termination under Clause 10.1, the Employer shall determine the value of the work executed and the materials and Plant delivered to the Site prior to the date of termination, and shall pay to the Contractor the amounts so determined less:

(a) any amounts previously paid to the Contractor;

(b) the value of any materials or Plant for which the Contractor has already been paid; and

(c) any additional costs and damages incurred by the Employer by reason of the termination, including the cost of completing the Works, which shall be deducted from any monies otherwise due to the Contractor, or if such costs and damages exceed the monies due, the Contractor shall pay the difference to the Employer.

10.5 The Contractor may terminate this Contract by written notice to the Employer if the Employer:

(a) fails to pay the Contractor any amount due under this Contract within forty-two (42) days after the due date, and such failure continues for a further fourteen (14) days after receipt of written notice from the Contractor;

(b) is in material breach of its obligations under this Contract and fails to remedy such breach within thirty (30) days after receipt of written notice from the Contractor; or

(c) suspends the Works for a continuous period of one hundred and eighty-two (182) days pursuant to Clause 12, other than as a result of the Contractor’s default.
